# 0015 — MiniMax on its Anthropic-compatible API
# Why: MiniMax recommends its Anthropic-compatible API for agents and tool use with M3.x
# (https://platform.minimax.io/docs/guides/text-m3-function-call.md, read 2026-11-18): tools, streaming, and thinking
# blocks that carry a signature and must come back unchanged on every later request of a tool loop
# (https://platform.minimax.io/docs/api-reference/text-anthropic-api). StarNet's CUSTOM provider only speaks the
# OpenAI-compatible wire. With this record, a custom endpoint whose address is a MiniMax host (minimax.io /
# minimaxi.com) at /anthropic or /anthropic/v1 runs on StarNet's own Anthropic adapter (signed thinking replay, cache
# breakpoints, Anthropic usage fields). Every other custom endpoint, and a MiniMax /v1 address, is unchanged
# (test/minimax-anthropic-wire.test.js). company/tools/lib/minimax-endpoint.js sends the /anthropic address only when
# this checkout's StarNet carries this record.
# Apply:  git -C starnet apply --3way company/patches/0015-minimax-anthropic-wire.diff ; then restart the station.
# Revert: git -C starnet apply -R company/patches/0015-minimax-anthropic-wire.diff ; then re-save the MiniMax
#         connection (Settings › Connections) so the station is back on the /v1 address, and restart the station.
